{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Sculpt Texture Brushes.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Sculpt Texture Brushes.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender sculpt texture brushes blender sculpt texture brushes","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Sculpt Texture Brushes.md","fileName":"Blender Sculpt Texture Brushes.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Sculpt Texture Brushes","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-07 23:25\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Sculpting and Geometry Objects]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Sculpting and Geometry Objects","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Sculpt Texture Brushes.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Sculpt Texture Brushes.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender sculpt texture brushes blender sculpt texture brushes","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Sculpt Texture Brushes.md","fileName":"Blender Sculpt Texture Brushes.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Sculpt Texture Brushes","heading":"Blender Sculpt Texture Brushes","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A texture can modulate a sculpt brush, replacing a uniform stroke with patterned surface detail. Existing textures from Texture Properties or the Texture Node Editor can be assigned through the brush's Texture panel.\n\nRake rotates the texture to follow the direction of the stroke, reducing repetitive stamped patterns. Textured brushes are therefore useful for adding detail while retaining the speed of broad brush-based sculpting.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Sculpting and Geometry Objects","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Sculpt Texture Brushes.md::2","sou